4222b28125d6bc1820","position":"1788494640608952876-612ce87d-8665-4177-a5ae-0295305bc7d1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-aa9e-3d35.","timestamp":1788469034333024001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BLOCKED before RED: docs/security.md is fully generated by scripts/gen_config_reference.py ('do not edit by hand'; drift test under make test enforces this). The ticket AC requires adding scanner-lock/update/recovery content to docs/security.md, but the generator that owns that file is outside declared file_impact. Per leaf protocol, stopping rather than editing outside scope.","timestamp":1788469088111957001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SCOPE CORRECTION (orchestrator): docs/security.md is FULLY GENERATED by\nscripts/gen_config_reference.py (carries a \"do not edit by hand\" banner; a drift test under\nmake test fails if stale). The generator already has a \"Curated narrative (security.md) — NOT\nregistry-derivable\" region (gen_config_reference.py:103), which is exactly where the AC's\nscanner-lock authority/checksum-provenance/bump/recovery procedure belongs. Added\nscripts/gen_config_reference.py + its drift tests (test_gen_config_reference.py,\ntest_generated_surface_markers.py) to file_impact; docs/security.md stays as the regenerated\noutput. Edit the generator's curated narrative and regenerate — do NOT hand-edit security.md. No\nother Wave-1 agent touches these files.","timestamp":1788469180510618647},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Revised plan after scope correction: docs/security.md content will be authored in scripts/gen_config_reference.py's curated security narrative, with generator-level docs oracle and drift-check proof before implementation.","timestamp":1788469791820384001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented pinned review scanner contracts in worktree janitor-aa9e-3d35. RED held-out oracle captured missing generated security docs, lock manifest, installer fallback/integrity, and workflow/vote wiring; GREEN after implementation; mutation killed by removing Gerrit scanner success requirement. Local gates: held-out+targeted 107 passed, lint/typecheck passed, scanner lock validation passed, scanner target rejects unsupported macOS host as expected. Full make test hit pre-existing lifecycle failure also reproduced on clean origin/main baseline.","timestamp":1788475914532693001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BLOCKED after Gerrit CI: change 2595 failed Verified on repository contract tests that require edits outside corrected file_impact: tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py (vote.needs route coverage), tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py (locked workflow-name table), and .github/mechanism-baseline.json or equivalent mechanism-baseline update path for new admitted scanner CI gates. Per leaf protocol, stopping rather than editing outside scope; Gerrit change marked WIP.","timestamp":1788478041211358001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 3 pushed to Gerrit change 2595 after fixing LLM advisory correctness in the scanner installer CLI: --install-dir is now honored consistently for install/check/PATH reporting, and --semgrep-venv is passed through to the semgrep installer. Added unit coverage for those CLI paths and the gitleaks archive-without-binary guard. Evidence before push: scanner-focused targeted suite + held-out oracle 176 passed; validate-locks and generated docs check passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed. Full sanitized make test is still running locally per operator-provided host override while CI gates patch set 3.","timestamp":1788488314118206514},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 4 pushed to Gerrit change 2595. Addressed remaining LLM advisory issues within scope: --check-only without a local archive now verifies installed scanner binaries using the selected prefix; gitleaks archive extraction now streams the named binary into the destination path instead of tar.extract metadata/path handling; added observable tests for check-only dispatch and nested-archive path stripping; replaced the workflow prose-substring assertion with a structural runs-on assertion. Evidence before push: targeted + held-out oracle 178 passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed.","timestamp":1788490644694452322},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2595 landed after green gates. Patch set 4 labels: LLM-Review +1 at 2026-09-04 03:27:22 UTC; Verified +1 at 2026-09-04 03:36:35 UTC from run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33831682168. Submitted successfully; Gerrit returned status MERGED for Change-Id I38dfbc1ae144642f52c86240941e3a19e87ae5eb. Residual advisory disposition: accepted for this leaf because LLM marked non-blocking and CI verified the strict pinned scanner contract; docs use checksums_url as provenance, not a runtime fetch; download timeout/scheme hardening and extra manifest-negative tests are improvement follow-ups rather than blockers for the hash-locked Verified lane.","timestamp":1788493028455907180}],"created_at":1788311614552960001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d9c746a6-7c13-4418-aa30-5801810cf136","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"ba86ab14-fa57-4e2a-bec9-197bad6654e8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aa9d-3f7a-71d6-41d3"},{"link_uuid":"fafa833e-d404-4f28-a0f3-81fceeb21e62","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2cfb-f6cf-dcb7-424a"},{"link_uuid":"0729a141-54c0-441a-b240-f6b4897bb6bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9317-fd35-a180-4083"},{"link_uuid":"59d40695-d0f9-4a34-9112-4a6ce60c1c09","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8495-71a1-c4b4-4b49"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nNine real scanner integration tests skip when binaries are absent at `tests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py:97-158`, `test_code_review_public_exposure.py:109-151`, and `test_code_review_ws5.py:347-399`. Verified installs neither scanner although `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:43-71` makes them runtime prerequisites. The review-bot is deployed on Linux/arm64 Graviton while Verified runs on Linux/amd64, so their scanner pins must be platform-aware.\n\n## Approach\n\nCreate one checked-in scanner lock manifest with separate `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` entries. Each entry records a Gitleaks version, its exact per-platform release URL, and SHA-256; the pinned checksum is taken from that release’s published `*_checksums.txt` asset at lock-update time. Each platform also references a fully resolved Semgrep requirements lock containing the same top-level Semgrep version and all platform-resolved distribution hashes. Provision Semgrep with `pip install --require-hashes`; do not represent this multi-wheel install as one fictional artifact hash.\n\nAdd one provisioning helper as the sole installation owner. It selects the manifest entry from Docker’s target OS/architecture or the CI runner’s actual OS/architecture, rejects an unsupported platform before installation, verifies the Gitleaks digest before extraction, and installs Semgrep only from the selected hash lock. The Graviton review-bot Docker build consumes `linux/arm64`; the Linux x64 reusable Verified lane consumes `linux/amd64`. Tests cover both selections rather than asserting that those different consumers share one binary artifact.\n\nThis deliberately supersedes dynamic-Gitleaks/latest and unpinned-Semgrep behavior. Stable per-release assets plus published checksums make reproducible, verified pins preferable; `docs/security.md` is generated, so the scanner-lock documentation is authored in `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`'s curated security narrative and then regenerated with `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py`. The regenerated `docs/security.md` identifies the manifest, the checksum source, platform-lock update procedure, and the recovery action for a withdrawn asset (move both platform entries to an available verified release). Include a concrete worked example: bump Gitleaks by reading the release `*_checksums.txt`, updating each platform URL/SHA pair, regenerating Semgrep requirement locks with `pip --require-hashes`, running the installer validation target, and regenerating `docs/security.md`.\n\nAdd an explicit native-binary Make target that fails before its focused contracts for an unsupported platform, missing scanner, wrong Gitleaks version/digest, or missing/bad Semgrep requirement hash. It runs the nine real integration contracts only when a supported platform entry is provisioned. The existing skip-with-reason behavior remains for default local tests and unsupported developer platforms. Invoke the target from a reusable parallel workflow used by mirror CI and exact-patchset Gerrit verification, including the job in `vote.needs`.\n\nDo not build Docker, install OpenGrep, or add this target to normal `make lint`/default local tests.\n\n## Scope\n\n- platform-aware scanner manifest, two Semgrep hash locks, and review-bot Dockerfile\n- shared provisioning helper and explicit Make target\n- scanner integration tests\n- reusable mirror/Gerrit workflow and Verified parity guard\n- `docs/security.md` scanner-lock ownership, update, checksum, and recovery procedure\n\n## Testing\n\nFirst prove the generated-document assumption: add a generator-level docs oracle that fails until `render_security()` emits the scanner-lock section, then prove the committed-doc drift check fails when the generator output changes without regenerating and passes after `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py`. Exercise manifest selection for Linux/amd64 and Linux/arm64, unsupported-platform rejection, missing Gitleaks, a bad Gitleaks SHA-256, a missing or bad Semgrep requirement hash, and wrong scanner versions. Prove valid selected locks pass the real Semgrep and Gitleaks contracts, that unsupported local platforms retain the skip-with-reason path, and that workflow wiring plus `vote.needs` parity hold.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The manifest has independent `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` scanner entries, each with an exact Gitleaks URL and SHA-256 sourced from the matching release `*_checksums.txt` asset.\n- [ ] The review-bot Docker build selects and validates the `linux/arm64` entry; the reusable Linux x64 CI lane selects and validates the `linux/amd64` entry.\n- [ ] Every platform entry points to a fully resolved Semgrep requirements lock with an identical top-level Semgrep version and all required distribution hashes; the installer uses `pip --require-hashes`.\n- [ ] The installer rejects an unsupported platform, missing scanner, wrong Gitleaks version/digest, and invalid Semgrep hash before it runs the focused contracts.\n- [ ] Valid selected scanner locks allow the explicit native-binary target to pass all nine real Semgrep/Gitleaks integration contracts.\n- [ ] Default local tests on unsupported platforms preserve the existing skip-with-reason behavior and do not provision scanners.\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` owns a curated scanner-lock security narrative; regenerated `docs/security.md` names the manifest as the update authority, the checksum source, a concrete per-platform bump example, and the withdrawn-asset recovery procedure.\n- [ ] One parallel reusable lane serves mirror CI and exact Gerrit patchsets and is required by the Verified vote.\n- [ ] A generator-level docs oracle proves the scanner-lock section appears in regenerated `docs/security.md`, and the existing drift check proves committed `docs/security.md` fails when generator content changes without regeneration and passes after regeneration.\n- [ ] OpenGrep, Docker-image builds, normal `make lint`, and default local tests remain outside scope.\n- [ ] The lane's expected cold-run cost is documented as approximately 1.5-3 runner-minutes without extending the existing 22-23 minute critical path when capacity is available.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/review-scanners.lock.json","reason":"platform-aware Gitleaks integrity + Semgrep lock references"},{"path":"infra/compose/review-scanners.linux-amd64.requirements.txt","reason":"hash-locked Semgrep distributions for Verified"},{"path":"infra/compose/review-scanners.linux-arm64.requirements.txt","reason":"hash-locked Semgrep distributions for the Graviton review-bot"},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot","reason":"select arm64 scanner entry via shared provisioner"},{"path":"scripts/install_review_scanners.py","reason":"shared deploy/CI platform selection + integrity enforcement"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"native-binary scanner integration target"},{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"docs/security.md is generator-owned; add scanner-lock curated-narrative section here (security.md is do-not-edit-by-hand, drift-tested)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"drift test for regenerated security.md"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py","reason":"generated-surface marker test for security.md"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py","reason":"run real pinned rule contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_public_exposure.py","reason":"run real pinned exposure contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"run Semgrep and Gitleaks integration contracts"},{"path":".github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml","reason":"reusable mirror/Gerrit scanner lane"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"invoke scanner lane on mirror CI"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"invoke exact-patchset lane and require it in vote aggregation"},{"path":"docs/security.md","reason":"regenerated output carrying the scanner-lock section"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py","reason":"vote.needs route coverage changes: the scanner lane is now required by the Verified vote, so the triage comment's aggregated-check routing must include it (AC: lane required by Verified vote)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py","reason":"locked workflow-name set changes: the new reusable scanner lane adds a workflow name (AC: one parallel reusable lane serves mirror CI and Gerrit patchsets)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","2cfb-f6cf-dcb7-424a"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","8495-71a1-c4b4-4b49"],["relates_to","9317-fd35-a180-4083"],["relates_to","aa9d-3f7a-71d6-41d3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"1182f71c-8ff7-4839-ac20-18b66c81a513","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","ci","security","rp14"],"ticket_id":"aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee","ticket_type":"story","title":"Run pinned deployed Semgrep and Gitleaks contracts in Verified","v